Z||000000||maryjane||12-18-2001||12:25 AM||||The sulfnbk.exe virus hoax has resurfaced again and is being passed around. Several people sent me an 'alert' about it today. Symantec has re-issued the info today. If you aren't familar with this one, the email has the usual baloney about a virus that can't be detected by Mcafee or Norton and is indicated by the presence of a file called<BR>sulfnbk.exe. It is a MS Windows file used to restore long file names. Don't delete it like two of my friends did, without even checking the anti-virus sites. Most on PFF are a little more savvy than that, but thought I would mention it anyway.||||reg||1
